/-!
# Serre vanishing over a quasi-compact base, with no Noetherian hypothesis

[Stacks, Tag 02O1] is proved unconditionally as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleTwistAcyclicity`
`.exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule`, but with a **Noetherian** base.
This file removes that hypothesis for the powers of the relatively ample module itself, at the
price of the two hypotheses [Stacks, Tag 0B5T] grants for exactly this purpose: that the morphism
is **flat** and of **finite presentation**.  The conclusion is: for `g : Y ⟶ T` proper, flat and
of finite presentation with `T` only quasi-compact and `M` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module ample
relative to `g`, there is a `d₀` with

`R ᵖ g_* (M ^⊗ d) = 0` for every `p > 0` and every `d ≥ d₀`,

one bound serving every positive degree.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleTwistLimitVanishing`
  `.exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule_of_isAffine`: the affine-base case,
  which is where the limit argument runs.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleTwistLimitVanishing`
  `.exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule`: the quasi-compact-base case.

## The argument

It is the source's limit descent, in four steps.

* **Reduce to an affine base.** Vanishing of a higher direct image is local on the base
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_of_isZero_restrict_cover`, with
  [Stacks, Tag 01E5] to compare the restriction of `R ᵖ g_*` with `R ᵖ (g ∣_ V)_*`), and a
  quasi-compact base has a **finite** affine open cover
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01XJUniformVanishing.exists_fin_affineOpen_cover`).  Finiteness is
  what lets the finitely many bounds be combined into one.  Over an affine open relative
  ampleness restricts to absolute ampleness and back by [Stacks, Tag 01VK].
* **Write the affine base as a limit of Noetherian affine bases.**
  `AlgebraicGeometry.affineStageCone` presents an affine `T` as the limit of the spectra of the
  subrings of `Γ(T, ⊤)` generated by
  finite subsets ([Stacks, Tag 01ZA]); every stage is affine, Noetherian and of finite type over
  `ℤ`, and every transition morphism is affine.
* **Descend the polarized family to a stage.** `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stage_polarizedModel`
  ([Stacks, Tag 0D43]) produces a stage `Tᵢ`, a proper, flat, finitely presented `gᵢ : Yᵢ ⟶ Tᵢ`
  carrying a relatively ample invertible `Lᵢ`, a cartesian square exhibiting `g` as its base
  change and an isomorphism `q^* Lᵢ ≅ M`.  The stage base is Noetherian, so [Stacks, Tag 02O1]
  applies there; it is taken with the structure sheaf as its coherent factor
  ([Stacks, Tag 01XZ]) and the unit factor is then cancelled by
  `Stacks.Algebraization.unitTensorModulesIso`.
* **Bring the vanishing back down.** This is the step that uses flatness, and it is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChangeVanishing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_pullback`
  of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FlatBaseChangeVanishing/Basic.lean`: because `gᵢ` is flat the
  square is Tor independent, so [Stacks, Tag 08IB] applies, and the vanishing of the higher direct
  images at the stage is inherited by the base change.  The transition morphism `T ⟶ Tᵢ` is
  neither flat nor Noetherian, and nothing is assumed of it.

## Implementation notes

**Three instances are supplied positionally.** `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stage_polarizedModel`
asks for `IsProper f` and `Flat f` at `f : X ⟶ c.pt`, and `(affineStageCone T).pt` is `T` only
after unfolding a projection, which instance search — which unifies at reducible transparency —
does not do.  The instances are therefore passed with `@`, where the term is checked at default
transparency.

`AlgebraicGeometry.FinitePresentation` is a conjunction rather than a class, so the finite
presentation of `g ∣_ V` is assembled from the three instances of its components.

`HasDerivedCategory.standard` is activated at priority `10000`, as in every file of this cluster.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D43](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D43)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ZA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ZA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08IB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01E5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01E5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XZ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.Ample Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleTwistLimitVanishing

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### Serre vanishing over an affine base -/

/-- **Serre vanishing over an affine base, with no Noetherian hypothesis.**  For `g : Y ⟶ T`
proper, flat and of finite presentation onto an affine base and `M` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module
ample relative to `g`, some `d₀` makes every higher direct image of `M ^⊗ d` vanish for `d ≥ d₀`.

`T` is presented as the limit of the spectra of the finitely generated subrings of `Γ(T, ⊤)`;
[Stacks, Tag 0D43] descends `(g, M)` to a stage, whose base is Noetherian, where
[Stacks, Tag 02O1] applies; and the vanishing comes back down because the square is Tor
independent, `g` being flat. -/
@[ega "III 2.4.1" "(ii), special case"]
theorem exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule_of_isAffine
    {Y T : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine T] (g : Y ⟶ T) [IsProper g] [Flat g]
    (hfp : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.FinitePresentation g)
    (M : Y.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule Y M]
    (hM : Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple g M) :
    ∃ d₀ : ℕ, ∀ d : ℕ, d₀ ≤ d → ∀ p : ℤ, 0 < p →
      IsZero (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward g).rightDerivedPlus p).obj
        (tensorPowModule Y M (d : ℤ))) := by
  -- The Noetherian approximation of the affine base `T`, with vertex `T` itself.  The three
  -- instances are supplied positionally: instance search unifies only at reducible transparency,
  -- where `(affineStageCone T).pt` and `T` do not meet.
  obtain ⟨i, Yi, gi, Li, hLiinv, q, hpr, hfl, hfpi, hampi, hpb, ⟨eL⟩⟩ :=
    @_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_stage_polarizedModel _ _ _
      (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.specAdjoinFinsetDiagram Γ(T, ⊤)) _
      (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.affineStageCone T)
      (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.isLimit_affineStageCone T) _ g ‹IsProper g› ‹Flat g› hfp M
      (‹IsInvertibleModule Y M›) hM
  have _hpr : IsProper gi := hpr
  have _hfl : Flat gi := hfl
  have _hLiinv : IsInvertibleModule Yi Li := hLiinv
  have _hLN : IsLocallyNoetherian Yi := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian gi
  have _hO : (unitModule Yi).IsCoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.structureSheaf_isCoherent Yi
  -- [Stacks, Tag 02O1] at the Noetherian stage, with the structure sheaf as the coherent factor.
  obtain ⟨n₀, hn₀⟩ :=
    AmpleTwistAcyclicity.exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule gi
      (unitModule Yi) Li hampi
  refine ⟨n₀, fun d hd p hp => ?_⟩
  -- The stage vanishing, with the unit factor cancelled.
  have hstage : ∀ j : ℤ, 0 < j → IsZero (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward gi).rightDerivedPlus j).obj
      (tensorPowModule Yi Li (d : ℤ))) := by
    intro j hj
    obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ : ∃ n : ℕ, j = (n : ℤ) := ⟨j.toNat, by omega⟩
    exact (hn₀ d j hd (by omega)).of_iso
      (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward gi).rightDerivedPlus j).mapIso
        (Stacks.Algebraization.unitTensorModulesIso Yi (tensorPowModule Yi Li (d : ℤ))).symm)
  -- Flat base change along the limit projection.
  have hbc :=
    _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChangeVanishing.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_pullback
      hpb (tensorPowModule Yi Li (d : ℤ))
      (Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuasicoherent_tensorPowModule Li (d : ℤ))
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFlat_of_isInvertible (X := Yi.toRingedSpace)
        (tensorPowModule Yi Li (d : ℤ)) inferInstance) hstage p hp
  -- `q^*(Li ^⊗ d) ≅ M ^⊗ d`.
  exact hbc.of_iso (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward g).rightDerivedPlus p).mapIso
    ((tensorPowModuleIsoOfIso Y ((modulePullback q.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj Li) M eL d).symm ≪≫
      (pullbackTensorPowModuleIso q Li d).symm))

/-! ### Serre vanishing over a quasi-compact base -/

/-- **Serre vanishing for the powers of a relatively ample invertible module over a
quasi-compact base, with no Noetherian hypothesis.**  For `g : Y ⟶ T` proper, flat and of finite
presentation with `T` quasi-compact and `M` an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module ample relative to `g`,
some `d₀` makes

`R ᵖ g_* (M ^⊗ d) = 0` for every `p > 0` and every `d ≥ d₀`,

with the one bound `d₀` serving every positive degree.

Vanishing of a higher direct image is local on the base, so a finite affine open cover of `T`
reduces this to the affine case above; the bound is the maximum of the finitely many bounds. -/
@[ega "III 2.4.1" "(ii), special case"]
theorem exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule
    {Y T : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace T] (g : Y ⟶ T) [IsProper g] [Flat g]
    (hfp : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.FinitePresentation g)
    (M : Y.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule Y M]
    (hM : Stacks.RelativeAmple.IsRelativelyAmple g M) :
    ∃ d₀ : ℕ, ∀ d : ℕ, d₀ ≤ d → ∀ p : ℤ, 0 < p →
      IsZero (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward g).rightDerivedPlus p).obj
        (tensorPowModule Y M (d : ℤ))) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨m, B, hBaff, hBcover⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag01XJUniformVanishing.exists_fin_affineOpen_cover T
  -- Over each member of the cover the affine case applies.
  have key : ∀ j : Fin m, ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ d : ℕ, n ≤ d → ∀ p : ℤ, 0 < p →
      IsZero (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (g ∣_ B j)).rightDerivedPlus p).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor (g ⁻¹ᵁ B j).ι).obj (tensorPowModule Y M (d : ℤ)))) := by
    intro j
    have : IsAffine (B j).toScheme := hBaff j
    have := hfp.1
    have := hfp.2.1
    have := hfp.2.2
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_isZero_rightDerivedPlus_pushforward_tensorPowModule_of_isAffine
      (g ∣_ B j) ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
      ((modulePullback (g ⁻¹ᵁ B j).ι.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj M)
      ((Stacks.RelativeAmpleAffineBase.isRelativelyAmple_iff_isAmple (g ∣_ B j) _).mpr
        (hM.2 (B j) (hBaff j)))
    exact ⟨n, fun d hd p hp => (hn d hd p hp).of_iso
      (((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (g ∣_ B j)).rightDerivedPlus p).mapIso
        ((Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctorIsoPullback (g ⁻¹ᵁ B j).ι).app
            (tensorPowModule Y M (d : ℤ)) ≪≫
          pullbackTensorPowModuleIso (g ⁻¹ᵁ B j).ι M d))⟩
  choose k hk using key
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.sup k, fun d hd p hp => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨pn, rfl⟩ : ∃ n : ℕ, p = (n : ℤ) := ⟨p.toNat, by omega⟩
  refine Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_of_isZero_restrict_cover B
    hBcover _ fun j => ?_
  exact (hk j d ((Finset.le_sup (f := k) (Finset.mem_univ j)).trans hd) (pn : ℤ) hp).of_iso
    (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveCoherentImage.higherDirectImageRestrictObjIso g (B j)
      (tensorPowModule Y M (d : ℤ)) pn).symm

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleTwistLimitVanishing

end
